A solitary crocodile resting motionless in murky swamp water at twilight, only its ancient eyes and ridged snout visible above the surface, reflecting golden light. The scene is rendered in Vincent van Gogh's distinctive style with swirling, expressive brushstrokes in deep teals, muddy ochres, and amber yellows. Cypress trees with characteristic spiraling forms line the distant shore, their reflections dancing in the water. The sky above churns with dynamic circular patterns in deepening purples and blues, suggesting both mystery and timeless wisdom. The crocodile's scales are rendered with thick, textured impasto strokes, giving them an almost sculptural quality. Spanish moss drapes from gnarled branches, painted with energetic curved lines. The overall mood conveys solitary intelligence, patient cunning, and primordial survival instinct.
